<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Morioka Domain</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1871 CE · capital Morioka</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The domain of the Nanbu family in northern Honshu, known for its horses and for the frequent famines and peasant uprisings of its cold lands.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanbu-clan">Nanbu</a> were an old warrior family of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutsu-province">Mutsu</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanbu-nobunao">Nanbu Nobunao</a> was confirmed in his lands by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> in 1590, though he lost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsugaru-clan">Tsugaru</a> region to a breakaway <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. He moved his seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morioka">Morioka</a>, where the castle was built in stages over several decades.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Assessed at 100,000 koku, later raised to 200,000 in 1808 to pay for guarding Ezo, the domain had poor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> yields and suffered repeated famines. It was famed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanbu-clan">Nanbu</a> horses and later for ironware. Heavy taxes provoked many peasant uprisings, culminating in the great Sanhei uprising of 1853, when thousands fled to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sendai-domain">Sendai Domain</a>. The feud with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsugaru-clan">Tsugaru</a> of Hirosaki lasted the whole period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morioka">Morioka</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ouetsu-reppan-domei">Ouetsu Reppan Domei</a> in 1868 and surrendered; it was briefly transferred and reduced. After abolition in 1871 it became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwate-prefecture">Iwate Prefecture</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/morioka-domain.jpg" alt="Morioka Domain" width="320" height="249"><figcaption>Image: Barfodt · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Nanbu_Lords_of_Morioka_in_Mutsu_Province_(A).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1871 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Morioka</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nanbu Nobunao, Nanbu Toshinao</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Japan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nanbu Domain</dd></dl></aside></div>
